{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EqibXcZ6VCsa1HFHfcZdJ7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — ec_hte_llm_annotation\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n5\t- Deadline: ARR submission May 25, 2026; commitment deadline August 2, 2026\n6\t- Format: Long paper, 8 pages + unlimited references\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条，可证伪)\n9\t\n10\t1. **Bias Mechanism Discovery**: When LLM misclassification rates for an effect modifier vary across subgroups, applying a global (pooled) correction to subgroup-level CATE estimates introduces systematic bias — over-correcting low-error subgroups and under-correcting high-error ones. In realistic settings, this \"debiasing\" can worsen CATE bias by 5-10x compared to no correction at all.\n11\t\n12\t2. **EC-HTE Solution**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified correction (EC-HTE) eliminates this bias while controlling estimation variance through partial pooling. MVP demonstrates near-zero subgroup-level bias with simple stratification; HB partial pooling (exp-001) expected to further reduce RMSE by controlling matrix-inversion variance. Applicable to any CATE estimator; demonstrated with difference-in-means and CausalForestDML.\n13\t\n14\t3. **Diagnostic Criterion**: The product of misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity across subgroups provides a computable diagnostic: when this product exceeds a threshold, global correction is harmful and stratified correction is needed. This criterion has standalone value independent of EC-HTE.\n15\t\n16\t## Story Spine\n17\t\n18\t- **Problem**: NLP researchers increasingly use LLM annotations as effect modifiers in heterogeneous treatment effect analysis (e.g., \"tweet contains economic framing\" moderates campaign effectiveness). LLM misclassification is non-random — error rates vary by subgroup (Ashwin et al., 2025: error varies by refugee status, gender, education). Current PPI/DSL corrections apply global rectifiers assuming homogeneous error.\n19\t\n20\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Mozer (2026) proves arm-specific rectifiers fix ATE bias under differential prediction error, but explicitly limits analysis to average treatment effects. PPI (Angelopoulos et al., 2023) and DSL (Egami et al., 2024) correct population-level estimates. PPCI (Sui et al., 2026) extends PPI to conditional functionals but corrects outcome-side measurement, not covariate-side. ForestIV (Bu et al., 2023) handles ML-covariate measurement error in regression, not CATE. **No work addresses correction when the mismeasured variable defines the heterogeneity structure.**\n21\t\n22\t- **Our framing**: We identify and formalize a previously unrecognized bias mechanism — measurement-error × causal-heterogeneity confounding. When a pooled confusion matrix is applied to correct subgroup-level CATEs, it misattributes prediction noise across subgroups with different error rates, producing bias proportional to the product of misclassification heterogeneity and CATE heterogeneity. This is a problem-level discovery, not a technique-level extension. EC-HTE solves it via hierarchical Bayesian stratified correction with honest causal forest integration. **Novelty positioning**: The individual components (HB Dirichlet estimation, confusion matrix correction, causal forests) are established; the contribution is (a) identifying and formalizing the bias mechanism specific to effect-modifier misclassification, (b) the Δπ×Δτ product characterization that predicts when correction backfires, and (c) bridging the measurement error and HTE literatures in a practically consequential way. Frame as \"problem identification + principled solution\" not \"new estimation technique.\"\n23\t\n24\t- **Headline result template**: \"On semi-synthetic political-science benchmarks, global correction worsens subgroup CATE bias by up to 7.8x in low-error subgroups; EC-HTE reduces bias to near-zero while maintaining 92-97% coverage, with as few as 250 expert labels.\"\n25\t\n26\t## Key Contributions (ordered for paper)\n27\t\n28\t1. **Bias mechanism identification + formal bound**: bias ∝ misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity. Includes \"debiasing can hurt\" proposition with constructive example. (Theory + Empirical)\n29\t2. **EC-HTE framework**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified misclassification correction + variance-adjusted honest causal forest. (Method)\n30\t3. **Diagnostic criterion**: Computable threshold from pilot data to decide whether stratified correction is needed. (Practical tool)\n31\t4. **Comprehensive validation**: Synthetic + semi-synthetic + real-data experiments with multiple LLMs. (Empirical)\n32\t\n33\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n34\t\n35\t1. **\"Why not just use expert labels directly for CATE?\"** — Defense: 2000 expert labels / k subgroups / honest forest halving → insufficient power per cell. EC-HTE uses all LLM data for low-variance CATE, expert labels only for calibration. Explicitly quantify in experiments.\n36\t\n37\t2. **\"How is this different from PPCI (Sui et al., 2026)?\"** — PPCI corrects outcome-side measurement error for conditional functionals via kernel localization. We correct covariate-side measurement error in the variable that defines the conditioning structure. Orthogonal problems.\n38\t\n39\t3. **\"Incremental over Mozer (2026)\"** — Mozer addresses ATE under differential prediction error. We address CATE under heterogeneous effect-modifier misclassification — a structurally different problem. The bias mechanism we identify (pooled correction hurting low-error subgroups) has no counterpart in Mozer's framework.\n40\t\n41\t4. **\"How sensitive to subgroup definition?\"** — Hierarchical Bayesian partial pooling makes the method robust: with well-defined subgroups, full stratification; with noisy subgroups, automatic shrinkage toward global. Include robustness analysis.\n42\t\n43\t5. **\"Real-world expert label cost\"** — Address with expert budget sensitivity sweep (n=100 to 2000) and adaptive allocation (Stage 3).\n44\t\n45\t6. **\"How does this differ from Carroll et al. (2006) / classical measurement error?\"** — Carroll et al. addresses measurement error in regression covariates; our contribution is the specific bias characterization for CATE estimation when the mismeasured variable *defines* the heterogeneity structure. The Δπ×Δτ product form is a new result in this context. Engage deeply with measurement error literature (Carroll, Gustafson, Hu & Schennach) and Bayesian annotation models (Dawid & Skene, Paun et al.) to contextualize precisely.\n46\t\n47\t7. **\"Methodological novelty is modest\"** — Acknowledge explicitly. Position contribution as problem discovery + formal characterization + comprehensive validation, not as a new estimation technique. The \"never worse than global\" guarantee via HB partial pooling is the key methodological property.\n48\t\n49\t8. **\"Why no figures?\"** — Paper MUST include key figures: (1) schematic of bias mechanism (global over/under-correction), (2) bias amplification heatmap (Δπ vs Δτ), (3) diagnostic ROC curve, (4) budget crossover curves. Move P2 experiments (exp-008, exp-009) to appendix to free space.\n50\t\n51\t## Venue Fit\n52\t\n53\tEMNLP fit is strong: core NLP application (LLM annotation quality), computational social science use case (political messaging, refugee interviews), direct comparison with NeurIPS/EMNLP published methods (DSL, PPI, benchmarking). Methodology is causal inference but framed through NLP lens. Potential reviewer pool: CL+CSS track.\n54\t\n55\tRisk: pure statistics reviewers may want stronger theoretical contribution (convergence rates, minimax bounds). Mitigation: emphasize the practical diagnostic criterion and empirical validation breadth.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37075016-2431-4308-9c0a-0827a1b2a63c","uuid":"88a46000-ed9a-4fcd-90c7-4df5e78b65e9","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:11:17.612Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T194535/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — ec_hte_llm_annotation\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Deadline: ARR submission May 25, 2026; commitment deadline August 2, 2026\n- Format: Long paper, 8 pages + unlimited references\n\n## Core Claims (3 条，可证伪)\n\n1. **Bias Mechanism Discovery**: When LLM misclassification rates for an effect modifier vary across subgroups, applying a global (pooled) correction to subgroup-level CATE estimates introduces systematic bias — over-correcting low-error subgroups and under-correcting high-error ones. In realistic settings, this \"debiasing\" can worsen CATE bias by 5-10x compared to no correction at all.\n\n2. **EC-HTE Solution**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified correction (EC-HTE) eliminates this bias while controlling estimation variance through partial pooling. MVP demonstrates near-zero subgroup-level bias with simple stratification; HB partial pooling (exp-001) expected to further reduce RMSE by controlling matrix-inversion variance. Applicable to any CATE estimator; demonstrated with difference-in-means and CausalForestDML.\n\n3. **Diagnostic Criterion**: The product of misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity across subgroups provides a computable diagnostic: when this product exceeds a threshold, global correction is harmful and stratified correction is needed. This criterion has standalone value independent of EC-HTE.\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: NLP researchers increasingly use LLM annotations as effect modifiers in heterogeneous treatment effect analysis (e.g., \"tweet contains economic framing\" moderates campaign effectiveness). LLM misclassification is non-random — error rates vary by subgroup (Ashwin et al., 2025: error varies by refugee status, gender, education). Current PPI/DSL corrections apply global rectifiers assuming homogeneous error.\n\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Mozer (2026) proves arm-specific rectifiers fix ATE bias under differential prediction error, but explicitly limits analysis to average treatment effects. PPI (Angelopoulos et al., 2023) and DSL (Egami et al., 2024) correct population-level estimates. PPCI (Sui et al., 2026) extends PPI to conditional functionals but corrects outcome-side measurement, not covariate-side. ForestIV (Bu et al., 2023) handles ML-covariate measurement error in regression, not CATE. **No work addresses correction when the mismeasured variable defines the heterogeneity structure.**\n\n- **Our framing**: We identify and formalize a previously unrecognized bias mechanism — measurement-error × causal-heterogeneity confounding. When a pooled confusion matrix is applied to correct subgroup-level CATEs, it misattributes prediction noise across subgroups with different error rates, producing bias proportional to the product of misclassification heterogeneity and CATE heterogeneity. This is a problem-level discovery, not a technique-level extension. EC-HTE solves it via hierarchical Bayesian stratified correction with honest causal forest integration. **Novelty positioning**: The individual components (HB Dirichlet estimation, confusion matrix correction, causal forests) are established; the contribution is (a) identifying and formalizing the bias mechanism specific to effect-modifier misclassification, (b) the Δπ×Δτ product characterization that predicts when correction backfires, and (c) bridging the measurement error and HTE literatures in a practically consequential way. Frame as \"problem identification + principled solution\" not \"new estimation technique.\"\n\n- **Headline result template**: \"On semi-synthetic political-science benchmarks, global correction worsens subgroup CATE bias by up to 7.8x in low-error subgroups; EC-HTE reduces bias to near-zero while maintaining 92-97% coverage, with as few as 250 expert labels.\"\n\n## Key Contributions (ordered for paper)\n\n1. **Bias mechanism identification + formal bound**: bias ∝ misclassification heterogeneity × CATE heterogeneity. Includes \"debiasing can hurt\" proposition with constructive example. (Theory + Empirical)\n2. **EC-HTE framework**: Hierarchical Bayesian subgroup-stratified misclassification correction + variance-adjusted honest causal forest. (Method)\n3. **Diagnostic criterion**: Computable threshold from pilot data to decide whether stratified correction is needed. (Practical tool)\n4. **Comprehensive validation**: Synthetic + semi-synthetic + real-data experiments with multiple LLMs. (Empirical)\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n1. **\"Why not just use expert labels directly for CATE?\"** — Defense: 2000 expert labels / k subgroups / honest forest halving → insufficient power per cell. EC-HTE uses all LLM data for low-variance CATE, expert labels only for calibration. Explicitly quantify in experiments.\n\n2. **\"How is this different from PPCI (Sui et al., 2026)?\"** — PPCI corrects outcome-side measurement error for conditional functionals via kernel localization. We correct covariate-side measurement error in the variable that defines the conditioning structure. Orthogonal problems.\n\n3. **\"Incremental over Mozer (2026)\"** — Mozer addresses ATE under differential prediction error. We address CATE under heterogeneous effect-modifier misclassification — a structurally different problem. The bias mechanism we identify (pooled correction hurting low-error subgroups) has no counterpart in Mozer's framework.\n\n4. **\"How sensitive to subgroup definition?\"** — Hierarchical Bayesian partial pooling makes the method robust: with well-defined subgroups, full stratification; with noisy subgroups, automatic shrinkage toward global. Include robustness analysis.\n\n5. **\"Real-world expert label cost\"** — Address with expert budget sensitivity sweep (n=100 to 2000) and adaptive allocation (Stage 3).\n\n6. **\"How does this differ from Carroll et al. (2006) / classical measurement error?\"** — Carroll et al. addresses measurement error in regression covariates; our contribution is the specific bias characterization for CATE estimation when the mismeasured variable *defines* the heterogeneity structure. The Δπ×Δτ product form is a new result in this context. Engage deeply with measurement error literature (Carroll, Gustafson, Hu & Schennach) and Bayesian annotation models (Dawid & Skene, Paun et al.) to contextualize precisely.\n\n7. **\"Methodological novelty is modest\"** — Acknowledge explicitly. Position contribution as problem discovery + formal characterization + comprehensive validation, not as a new estimation technique. The \"never worse than global\" guarantee via HB partial pooling is the key methodological property.\n\n8. **\"Why no figures?\"** — Paper MUST include key figures: (1) schematic of bias mechanism (global over/under-correction), (2) bias amplification heatmap (Δπ vs Δτ), (3) diagnostic ROC curve, (4) budget crossover curves. Move P2 experiments (exp-008, exp-009) to appendix to free space.\n\n## Venue Fit\n\nEMNLP fit is strong: core NLP application (LLM annotation quality), computational social science use case (political messaging, refugee interviews), direct comparison with NeurIPS/EMNLP published methods (DSL, PPI, benchmarking). Methodology is causal inference but framed through NLP lens. Potential reviewer pool: CL+CSS track.\n\nRisk: pure statistics reviewers may want stronger theoretical contribution (convergence rates, minimax bounds). Mitigation: emphasize the practical diagnostic criterion and empirical validation breadth.\n","numLines":56,"startLine":1,"totalLines":56}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011GywaPh6veCxFjaJcikDL9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"HB Dirichlet partial pooling vs MLE/Laplace stratified correction， full regime sweep (extreme/moderate/homogeneous × n_expert 100–2000 × K=2,4)。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"hb_rmse_vs_mle_extreme_k2_n250\": -0.02,\n7\t      \"hb_rmse_vs_mle_extreme_k2_n1000\": -0.01,\n8\t      \"hb_rmse_vs_mle_moderate_k2_n250\": 0.0,\n9\t      \"hb_rmse_vs_mle_moderate_k4_n250\": 0.03,\n10\t      \"hb_rmse_vs_mle_homogeneous_k2_n250\": 0.01,\n11\t      \"hb_coverage_95ci_extreme_k2_n250\": 0.86,\n12\t      \"hb_coverage_95ci_extreme_k2_n1000\": 0.91,\n13\t      \"hb_coverage_95ci_moderate_k2_n250\": 0.84,\n14\t      \"hb_coverage_95ci_moderate_k4_n250\": 0.83,\n15\t      \"hb_coverage_95ci_homogeneous_k2_n250\": 0.88,\n16\t      \"mle_coverage_95ci_extreme_k2_n250\": 0.82,\n17\t      \"mle_coverage_95ci_moderate_k4_n250\": 0.79,\n18\t      \"partial_pooling_shrinkage_factor_moderate_k4\": 0.65,\n19\t      \"mcmc_rhat_max\": 1.003,\n20\t      \"mcmc_ess_min\": 280,\n21\t      \"mcmc_runtime_vs_mle_ratio\": 45.0,\n22\t      \"mc_runs\": 1000\n23\t    },\n24\t    \"tables\": [\n25\t      {\n26\t        \"title\": \"Table 1: HB vs MLE Stratified — RMSE and Coverage by Regime\",\n27\t        \"columns\": [\n28\t          \"regime\",\n29\t          \"K\",\n30\t          \"n_expert\",\n31\t          \"rmse_hb\",\n32\t          \"rmse_mle\",\n33\t          \"rmse_diff_pct\",\n34\t          \"coverage_hb\",\n35\t          \"coverage_mle\"\n36\t        ],\n37\t        \"rows\": [\n38\t          [\n39\t            \"extreme\",\n40\t            2,\n41\t            250,\n42\t            0.041,\n43\t            0.042,\n44\t            \"-2.4%\",\n45\t            0.86,\n46\t            0.82\n47\t          ],\n48\t          [\n49\t            \"extreme\",\n50\t            2,\n51\t            1000,\n52\t            0.022,\n53\t            0.022,\n54\t            \"-1.0%\",\n55\t            0.91,\n56\t            0.89\n57\t          ],\n58\t          [\n59\t            \"extreme\",\n60\t            4,\n61\t            250,\n62\t            0.058,\n63\t            0.055,\n64\t            \"+5.5%\",\n65\t            0.83,\n66\t            0.8\n67\t          ],\n68\t          [\n69\t            \"moderate\",\n70\t            2,\n71\t            250,\n72\t            0.035,\n73\t            0.035,\n74\t            \"0.0%\",\n75\t            0.84,\n76\t            0.83\n77\t          ],\n78\t          [\n79\t            \"moderate\",\n80\t            2,\n81\t            1000,\n82\t            0.019,\n83\t            0.019,\n84\t            \"0.0%\",\n85\t            0.9,\n86\t            0.89\n87\t          ],\n88\t          [\n89\t            \"moderate\",\n90\t            4,\n91\t            250,\n92\t            0.049,\n93\t            0.048,\n94\t            \"+2.1%\",\n95\t            0.83,\n96\t            0.79\n97\t          ],\n98\t          [\n99\t            \"homogeneous\",\n100\t            2,\n101\t            250,\n102\t            0.03,\n103\t            0.03,\n104\t            \"+1.0%\",\n105\t            0.88,\n106\t            0.87\n107\t          ],\n108\t          [\n109\t            \"homogeneous\",\n110\t            4,\n111\t            250,\n112\t            0.038,\n113\t            0.037,\n114\t            \"+2.7%\",\n115\t            0.85,\n116\t            0.84\n117\t          ]\n118\t        ]\n119\t      },\n120\t      {\n121\t        \"title\": \"Table 2: MCMC Diagnostics Summary\",\n122\t        \"columns\": [\n123\t          \"parameter_group\",\n124\t          \"rhat_median\",\n125\t          \"rhat_max\",\n126\t          \"ess_bulk_min\",\n127\t          \"ess_tail_min\",\n128\t          \"runtime_sec\"\n129\t        ],\n130\t        \"rows\": [\n131\t          [\n132\t            \"confusion_matrix_k2\",\n133\t            1.001,\n134\t            1.003,\n135\t            450,\n136\t            280,\n137\t            42\n138\t          ],\n139\t          [\n140\t            \"confusion_matrix_k4\",\n141\t            1.002,\n142\t            1.005,\n143\t            320,\n144\t            210,\n145\t            185\n146\t          ],\n147\t          [\n148\t            \"cate_posterior_k2\",\n149\t            1.001,\n150\t            1.002,\n151\t            520,\n152\t            310,\n153\t            \"-\"\n154\t          ],\n155\t          [\n156\t            \"cate_posterior_k4\",\n157\t            1.002,\n158\t            1.004,\n159\t            380,\n160\t            240,\n161\t            \"-\"\n162\t          ]\n163\t        ]\n164\t      }\n165\t    ],\n166\t    \"figures\": [],\n167\t    \"analysis\": \"HB partial pooling 在 worst 档下不是 selling point。extreme regime 的微弱优势无法外推到 realistic 数据。Coverage 偏低是结构性问题——需要 bootstrap 或 sandwich variance 补救， 但这会进一步增加计算成本。论文中应诚实报告 HB 的边际价值有限，将贡献重心转向 bias mechanism 的 characterization 而非 estimation method。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 HB 与 MLE stratified 差异不显著。原因：partial pooling 的价值在于 borrowing strength across subgroups，但当 heterogeneity 本身不大时，MLE stratified 估计已经足够准确，Dirichlet prior 的 shrinkage 几乎无事可做。在 extreme regime（人造的 5x+ heterogeneity）下 HB 略优（RMSE 降 2%）， 但这个 regime 在 realistic 数据上不出现。moderate regime 下差异 < 1%。K=4 时 HB 反而略差（+3%）， 因为 Dirichlet 的 4×4 confusion matrix 参数空间更大，prior 选择更敏感，且 n_expert=250 时 每 cell 样本不足。Coverage 系统性偏低（83–88%），源于 confusion matrix 估计的 sampling uncertainty 未被充分传播到 CATE CI 中——posterior predictive intervals 低估了矩阵逆运算 中的 error propagation。MCMC 收敛良好但 runtime 是 MLE 的 45 倍，reviewer 会质疑实用性。\\n\"\n168\t  },\n169\t  {\n170\t    \"name\": \"Formal Bias Bound Verification\",\n171\t    \"description\": \"解析推导 bias = f(Δπ, Δτ)，K=2 和 K>2 两种情况。 MC 验证 analytic prediction vs empirical bias 的 R²。\\n\",\n172\t    \"results\": {\n173\t      \"analytic_r_squared_k2\": 0.92,\n174\t      \"analytic_r_squared_k4\": 0.68,\n175\t      \"analytic_r_squared_k8\": 0.52,\n176\t      \"bound_tightness_ratio_k2\": 1.15,\n177\t      \"bound_tightness_ratio_k4\": 2.3,\n178\t      \"bound_tightness_ratio_k8\": 3.8,\n179\t      \"bias_amplification_at_realistic_delta_pi_0p05\": 1.08,\n180\t      \"bias_amplification_at_realistic_delta_pi_0p10\": 1.18,\n181\t      \"bias_amplification_at_realistic_delta_pi_0p20\": 1.45,\n182\t      \"bias_amplification_at_extreme_delta_pi_0p40\": 3.2,\n183\t      \"debiasing_hurts_threshold_delta_pi\": 0.08,\n184\t      \"mc_ci_width_bias_estimate\": 0.003\n185\t    },\n186\t    \"tables\": [\n187\t      {\n188\t        \"title\": \"Table 3: Analytic Bound Accuracy by K\",\n189\t        \"columns\": [\n190\t          \"K\",\n191\t          \"r_squared\",\n192\t          \"bound_tightness_ratio\",\n193\t          \"n_mc_runs\"\n194\t        ],\n195\t        \"rows\": [\n196\t          [\n197\t            2,\n198\t            0.92,\n199\t            1.15,\n200\t            1000\n201\t          ],\n202\t          [\n203\t            4,\n204\t            0.68,\n205\t            2.3,\n206\t            1000\n207\t          ],\n208\t          [\n209\t            8,\n210\t            0.52,\n211\t            3.8,\n212\t            500\n213\t          ]\n214\t        ]\n215\t      },\n216\t      {\n217\t        \"title\": \"Table 4: Bias Amplification (Global/No-Correction) by Δπ\",\n218\t        \"columns\": [\n219\t          \"delta_pi\",\n220\t          \"delta_tau\",\n221\t          \"bias_amplification_k2\",\n222\t          \"bias_amplification_k4\"\n223\t        ],\n224\t        \"rows\": [\n225\t          [\n226\t            0.05,\n227\t            0.3,\n228\t            1.08,\n229\t            1.12\n230\t          ],\n231\t          [\n232\t            0.1,\n233\t            0.3,\n234\t            1.18,\n235\t            1.25\n236\t          ],\n237\t          [\n238\t            0.2,\n239\t            0.3,\n240\t            1.45,\n241\t            1.62\n242\t          ],\n243\t          [\n244\t            0.4,\n245\t            0.3,\n246\t            3.2,\n247\t            4.1\n248\t          ],\n249\t          [\n250\t            0.05,\n251\t            0.6,\n252\t            1.15,\n253\t            1.2\n254\t          ],\n255\t          [\n256\t            0.1,\n257\t            0.6,\n258\t            1.35,\n259\t            1.48\n260\t          ],\n261\t          [\n262\t            0.2,\n263\t            0.6,\n264\t            2.1,\n265\t            2.55\n266\t          ]\n267\t        ]\n268\t      }\n269\t    ],\n270\t    \"figures\": [],\n271\t    \"analysis\": \"Δπ×Δτ bound 在 K=2 时优雅且 tight，但 generalization 到 K>2 失败——这是 worst 档的 核心问题。论文不能宣称 \\\"通用诊断准则\\\"，只能说 \\\"K=2 的 exact characterization + K>2 的 conservative sufficient condition\\\"。Realistic parameter 区间内 bias amplification 太小， \\\"debiasing can hurt by 5–10x\\\" 的 headline 只在人造 extreme regime 成立。需要 reframe： \\\"我们证明了在何种条件下问题才会严重，并发现当前 LLM 通常不触发这些条件。\\\"\\n\\n\\nK=2 时 Δπ×Δτ 形式是 exact（R²=0.92，残差来自 finite-sample noise），因为二分类 confusion matrix 只有一个自由度，bias 表达式可以 closed-form 展开。但 K>2 时 confusion matrix 是 K×K，交叉项爆炸——K=4 有 12 个 off-diagonal 元素，Δπ×Δτ 的简单乘积形式只是 first-order approximation，忽略了 cross-subgroup misclassification 的高阶交互。R² 从 0.92（K=2） 降到 0.68（K=4）再到 0.52（K=8），bound 变得越来越松（tightness ratio 从 1.15 到 3.8）。 在 realistic Δπ 范围（0.05–0.10，对应 LLM 在不同 subgroup 间 5–10pp 的 accuracy 差异）， bias amplification 仅 1.08–1.18x，不构成实际危害。只有在 Δπ≥0.20 时才开始显著（1.45x）， 而这个水平在当前 LLM 上很少见。\\\"Debiasing can hurt\\\" 的 threshold 虽然存在（Δπ≈0.08）， 但 hurt 的程度很小。\\n\"\n272\t  },\n273\t  {\n274\t    \"name\": \"Semi-Synthetic Benchmark\",\n275\t    \"description\": \"Real tweet corpus + injected CATE structure + GPT-4.1/Qwen3-235B 标注。 测量 real misclassification heterogeneity，EC-HTE vs global vs no-correction。\\n\",\n276\t    \"results\": {\n277\t      \"gpt4_misclass_heterogeneity_max_min_ratio\": 1.12,\n278\t      \"qwen3_misclass_heterogeneity_max_min_ratio\": 1.18,\n279\t      \"gpt4_overall_accuracy\": 0.88,\n280\t      \"qwen3_overall_accuracy\": 0.82,\n281\t      \"ec_hte_subgroup_bias_reduction_vs_global_gpt4\": 0.25,\n282\t      \"ec_hte_subgroup_bias_reduction_vs_global_qwen3\": 0.4,\n283\t      \"global_vs_nocorrection_bias_amplification_gpt4\": 1.05,\n284\t      \"global_vs_nocorrection_bias_amplification_qwen3\": 1.12,\n285\t      \"ec_hte_coverage_95ci_gpt4\": 0.87,\n286\t      \"ec_hte_coverage_95ci_qwen3\": 0.85,\n287\t      \"global_coverage_95ci_gpt4\": 0.85,\n288\t      \"global_coverage_95ci_qwen3\": 0.82,\n289\t      \"nocorrection_coverage_95ci_gpt4\": 0.78,\n290\t      \"nocorrection_coverage_95ci_qwen3\": 0.74,\n291\t      \"max_subgroup_bias_global_gpt4\": 0.015,\n292\t      \"max_subgroup_bias_global_qwen3\": 0.028,\n293\t      \"max_subgroup_bias_echte_gpt4\": 0.011,\n294\t      \"max_subgroup_bias_echte_qwen3\": 0.017\n295\t    },\n296\t    \"tables\": [\n297\t      {\n298\t        \"title\": \"Table 5: Misclassification Heterogeneity — Real LLM on Semi-Synthetic Data\",\n299\t        \"columns\": [\n300\t          \"llm\",\n301\t          \"overall_acc\",\n302\t          \"subgroup_acc_min\",\n303\t          \"subgroup_acc_max\",\n304\t          \"max_min_ratio\"\n305\t        ],\n306\t        \"rows\": [\n307\t          [\n308\t            \"GPT-4.1\",\n309\t            0.88,\n310\t            0.86,\n311\t            0.9,\n312\t            1.12\n313\t          ],\n314\t          [\n315\t            \"Qwen3-235B\",\n316\t            0.82,\n317\t            0.78,\n318\t            0.86,\n319\t            1.18\n320\t          ]\n321\t        ]\n322\t      },\n323\t      {\n324\t        \"title\": \"Table 6: Subgroup CATE Bias (Max Across Subgroups)\",\n325\t        \"columns\": [\n326\t          \"method\",\n327\t          \"gpt4_max_bias\",\n328\t          \"gpt4_mean_bias\",\n329\t          \"qwen3_max_bias\",\n330\t          \"qwen3_mean_bias\"\n331\t        ],\n332\t        \"rows\": [\n333\t          [\n334\t            \"No Correction\",\n335\t            0.025,\n336\t            0.018,\n337\t            0.042,\n338\t            0.03\n339\t          ],\n340\t          [\n341\t            \"Global Correction\",\n342\t            0.015,\n343\t            0.01,\n344\t            0.028,\n345\t            0.019\n346\t          ],\n347\t          [\n348\t            \"EC-HTE (MLE)\",\n349\t            0.012,\n350\t            0.008,\n351\t            0.018,\n352\t            0.012\n353\t          ],\n354\t          [\n355\t            \"EC-HTE (HB)\",\n356\t            0.011,\n357\t            0.008,\n358\t            0.017,\n359\t            0.011\n360\t          ]\n361\t        ]\n362\t      }\n363\t    ],\n364\t    \"figures\": [],\n365\t    \"analysis\": \"Semi-synthetic 结果是 worst 档叙事的核心证据：real LLM 的 misclassification heterogeneity 不足以让 global correction 失效。EC-HTE 有微弱优势但 \\\"insurance, not necessity\\\"。 论文 framing 必须转向 Angle A：\\\"好消息是当前 LLM 通常不触发这个问题\\\"。 Qwen3 比 GPT-4.1 heterogeneity 略大，暗示 weaker LLMs 可能在某些 domain 触发—— 这为 exp-008 寻找 stronger case 提供方向。\\n\\n\\nReal LLM 数据上 misclassification heterogeneity 远低于 synthetic extreme regime。 GPT-4.1 accuracy 高（88%）且跨 subgroup 差异小（max/min ratio 1.12），因为 frontier LLM 在 political text 分类上已经足够好，不同 subgroup 的语言难度差异被模型能力压平。Qwen3 稍差 （82%, ratio 1.18），但仍远低于 \\\"5x\\\" 的 extreme 设定。结果：global correction 几乎不 hurt （amplification 1.05–1.12x），EC-HTE 的 bias reduction 有但幅度小（25–40%），绝对 bias 差异在 0.004–0.011 之间——统计上可能显著但实际上微不足道。Coverage 偏低延续了 exp-001 的 pattern。这个结果直接动摇 Claim 1 的 \\\"practically consequential\\\" 部分。\\n\"\n366\t  },\n367\t  {\n368\t    \"name\": \"Ashwin et al. Real-Data Validation\",\n369\t    \"description\": \"Rohingya refugee interview 数据，LLM 标注 error 与 refugee status/gender/education 相关。 EC-HTE vs global correction on real CATEs。\\n\",\n370\t    \"results\": {\n371\t      \"misclass_heterogeneity_max_min_ratio\": 1.22,\n372\t      \"ec_hte_cate_shift_vs_global_max_subgroup\": 0.035,\n373\t      \"ec_hte_cate_shift_vs_global_mean\": 0.018,\n374\t      \"ec_hte_coverage\": 0.86,\n375\t      \"global_coverage\": 0.83,\n376\t      \"nocorrection_coverage\": 0.76,\n377\t      \"bias_amplification_global_vs_nocorrection\": 1.15,\n378\t      \"qualitative_conclusion_changes\": 0\n379\t    },\n380\t    \"tables\": [\n381\t      {\n382\t        \"title\": \"Table 7: Ashwin et al. — Misclassification by Subgroup\",\n383\t        \"columns\": [\n384\t          \"subgroup\",\n385\t          \"n\",\n386\t          \"llm_accuracy\",\n387\t          \"accuracy_se\"\n388\t        ],\n389\t        \"rows\": [\n390\t          [\n391\t            \"female_refugee\",\n392\t            420,\n393\t            0.78,\n394\t            0.02\n395\t          ],\n396\t          [\n397\t            \"male_refugee\",\n398\t            380,\n399\t            0.82,\n400\t            0.02\n401\t          ],\n402\t          [\n403\t            \"female_host\",\n404\t            350,\n405\t            0.88,\n406\t            0.017\n407\t          ],\n408\t          [\n409\t            \"male_host\",\n410\t            310,\n411\t            0.9,\n412\t            0.017\n413\t          ]\n414\t        ]\n415\t      },\n416\t      {\n417\t        \"title\": \"Table 8: CATE Estimates by Method\",\n418\t        \"columns\": [\n419\t          \"subgroup\",\n420\t          \"cate_nocorr\",\n421\t          \"cate_global\",\n422\t          \"cate_echte\",\n423\t          \"shift_global_to_echte\"\n424\t        ],\n425\t        \"rows\": [\n426\t          [\n427\t            \"female_refugee\",\n428\t            0.142,\n429\t            0.158,\n430\t            0.172,\n431\t            0.014\n432\t          ],\n433\t          [\n434\t            \"male_refugee\",\n435\t            0.118,\n436\t            0.131,\n437\t            0.138,\n438\t            0.007\n439\t          ],\n440\t          [\n441\t            \"female_host\",\n442\t            0.085,\n443\t            0.094,\n444\t            0.09,\n445\t            -0.004\n446\t          ],\n447\t          [\n448\t            \"male_host\",\n449\t            0.062,\n450\t            0.069,\n451\t            0.065,\n452\t            -0.004\n453\t          ]\n454\t        ]\n455\t      }\n456\t    ],\n457\t    \"figures\": [],\n458\t    \"analysis\": \"Real data 上 EC-HTE 有方向性的 correction 但幅度不足以改变结论。没有 ground truth 是致命 弱点——无法证明 EC-HTE 更接近 truth 还是引入了 overcorrection。论文只能定性地论证 \\\"stratified correction 的方向与 known error patterns 一致\\\"。作为 supporting evidence 可以放在论文中，但不能作为 standalone claim 的证据。\\n\\n\\nAshwin et al. 数据的优势是 known demographic-correlated error，但 refugee interview text 的 LLM 分类难度差异（按 refugee status/gender）可能只是 moderate。max/min ratio 1.22 比 semi-synthetic 高一些（因为 code-switching、方言、文化特定表达确实影响 LLM），但仍不到 dramatic 的程度。EC-HTE 的 CATE 调整量（0.035）虽然比 semi-synthetic 大，但没有改变任何 subgroup 的 qualitative conclusion（即哪个 subgroup 的 treatment effect 更大的排序不变）。 这意味着 EC-HTE 在实际决策层面没有 impact。Coverage 稍好于 semi-synthetic 但仍低于 nominal。 无 ground truth CATE 导致无法计算 bias——只能报告 \\\"correction shift\\\"，reviewer 可能质疑 这是 improvement 还是 overcorrection。\\n\"\n459\t  },\n460\t  {\n461\t    \"name\": \"Diagnostic Criterion Validation\",\n462\t    \"description\": \"Δπ×Δτ product 作为 diagnostic，ROC 分析预测 \\\"global correction harmful\\\" 的准确性。\\n\",\n463\t    \"results\": {\n464\t      \"diagnostic_auc_k2\": 0.74,\n465\t      \"diagnostic_auc_k4\": 0.65,\n466\t      \"diagnostic_auc_overall\": 0.7,\n467\t      \"optimal_threshold_delta_pi_times_delta_tau\": 0.025,\n468\t      \"sensitivity_at_fpr_0p10\": 0.52,\n469\t      \"specificity_at_tpr_0p90\": 0.35,\n470\t      \"fraction_settings_where_global_harmful\": 0.18\n471\t    },\n472\t    \"tables\": [\n473\t      {\n474\t        \"title\": \"Table 9: Diagnostic ROC Summary\",\n475\t        \"columns\": [\n476\t          \"setting\",\n477\t          \"auc\",\n478\t          \"sensitivity_at_fpr10\",\n479\t          \"specificity_at_tpr90\",\n480\t          \"n_settings\"\n481\t        ],\n482\t        \"rows\": [\n483\t          [\n484\t            \"K=2 synthetic\",\n485\t            0.74,\n486\t            0.58,\n487\t            0.42,\n488\t            500\n489\t          ],\n490\t          [\n491\t            \"K=4 synthetic\",\n492\t            0.65,\n493\t            0.45,\n494\t            0.28,\n495\t            500\n496\t          ],\n497\t          [\n498\t            \"semi-synthetic (GPT-4.1)\",\n499\t            0.71,\n500\t            0.5,\n501\t            0.33,\n502\t            100\n503\t          ],\n504\t          [\n505\t            \"semi-synthetic (Qwen3)\",\n506\t            0.73,\n507\t            0.55,\n508\t            0.38,\n509\t            100\n510\t          ],\n511\t          [\n512\t            \"overall\",\n513\t            0.7,\n514\t            0.52,\n515\t            0.35,\n516\t            1200\n517\t          ]\n518\t        ]\n519\t      }\n520\t    ],\n521\t    \"figures\": [],\n522\t    \"analysis\": \"AUC < 0.75 意味着 Claim 3（diagnostic criterion）作为 standalone contribution 失败。 不能推荐给 practitioners 说 \\\"用这个判断是否需要 stratified correction\\\"。但问题的 formalization 本身仍有价值——\\\"什么情况下应该担心\\\" 的问题此前无人提出。论文中 reframe 为 \\\"we provide a conservative sufficient condition, not a precise diagnostic\\\"：如果 Δπ×Δτ > threshold， 一定要用 stratified；如果 < threshold，大概率 safe 但不保证。这在 Angle A 叙事下 work。\\n\\n\\nDiagnostic AUC 受限于两个因素。(1) \\\"Global correction harmful\\\" 的 base rate 低（仅 18% 的 settings 触发），因为 realistic parameter 空间中 Δπ 和 Δτ 都倾向于小值——大多数时候 global correction 是 fine 的。低 base rate 让 classifier 难以 distinguish。(2) K>2 时 Δπ×Δτ 本身就不是好的 summary statistic（exp-002 已证明），sum-of-products 形式有 information loss。AUC=0.70 意味着 diagnostic 比随机好但远不够 reliable——sensitivity 和 specificity 无法同时高。作为 \\\"practical tool\\\" 推荐给用户是勉强的。\\n\"\n523\t  },\n524\t  {\n525\t    \"name\": \"Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\",\n526\t    \"description\": \"n_expert sweep {50, 100, 250, 500, 1000, 2000} × K ∈ {2, 4, 8}， 找 EC-HTE > Global 的 crossover point。\\n\",\n527\t    \"results\": {\n528\t      \"crossover_n_k2_moderate\": 750,\n529\t      \"crossover_n_k4_moderate\": \"never (within 2000)\",\n530\t      \"crossover_n_k2_extreme\": 350,\n531\t      \"crossover_n_k8_moderate\": \"never (within 2000)\",\n532\t      \"hb_advantage_at_n250_k2_moderate_rmse_pct\": -1.5,\n533\t      \"hb_advantage_at_n250_k4_moderate_rmse_pct\": 4.0,\n534\t      \"hb_advantage_at_n1000_k2_moderate_rmse_pct\": -0.5,\n535\t      \"ec_hte_rmse_at_n50_k2\": 0.095,\n536\t      \"ec_hte_rmse_at_n100_k2\": 0.068,\n537\t      \"ec_hte_rmse_at_n2000_k2\": 0.018,\n538\t      \"global_rmse_at_n50_k2\": 0.052,\n539\t      \"global_rmse_at_n2000_k2\": 0.019\n540\t    },\n541\t    \"tables\": [\n542\t      {\n543\t        \"title\": \"Table 10: Budget Crossover Analysis\",\n544\t        \"columns\": [\n545\t          \"K\",\n546\t          \"regime\",\n547\t          \"crossover_n\",\n548\t          \"ec_hte_rmse_at_crossover\",\n549\t          \"global_rmse_at_crossover\"\n550\t        ],\n551\t        \"rows\": [\n552\t          [\n553\t            2,\n554\t            \"extreme\",\n555\t            350,\n556\t            0.032,\n557\t            0.032\n558\t          ],\n559\t          [\n560\t            2,\n561\t            \"moderate\",\n562\t            750,\n563\t            0.024,\n564\t            0.024\n565\t          ],\n566\t          [\n567\t            2,\n568\t            \"homogeneous\",\n569\t            \">2000\",\n570\t            \"-\",\n571\t            \"-\"\n572\t          ],\n573\t          [\n574\t            4,\n575\t            \"extreme\",\n576\t            650,\n577\t            0.045,\n578\t            0.045\n579\t          ],\n580\t          [\n581\t            4,\n582\t            \"moderate\",\n583\t            \">2000\",\n584\t            \"-\",\n585\t            \"-\"\n586\t          ],\n587\t          [\n588\t            8,\n589\t            \"extreme\",\n590\t            1200,\n591\t            0.068,\n592\t            0.068\n593\t          ],\n594\t          [\n595\t            8,\n596\t            \"moderate\",\n597\t            \">2000\",\n598\t            \"-\",\n599\t            \"-\"\n600\t          ]\n601\t        ]\n602\t      }\n603\t    ],\n604\t    \"figures\": [],\n605\t    \"analysis\": \"Budget sensitivity 是 worst 档的另一个 pain point。EC-HTE 在 realistic settings 下需要 大量 expert labels 才能 justify——这与 \\\"reduce expert labeling burden\\\" 的叙事矛盾。 论文需要诚实报告：EC-HTE 是 insurance policy，只在高 heterogeneity 时 pay off， 且 cost 随 K 快速增长。建议将 K=2 作为主结果，K≥4 放 appendix 并讨论 limitations。\\n\\n\\nCrossover point 高（500–1000 range）因为 EC-HTE 需要足够 per-subgroup expert labels 来 估计 K×K confusion matrix——K=2 时每个 cell 需要 ~50 个 labels 才 stable，意味着总共需要 ~200+。但在 moderate heterogeneity 下 global 的 bias 很小，EC-HTE 的 variance cost（来自 subgroup-level estimation）直到 n=750 才被 bias reduction 补偿。K=4 和 K=8 在 moderate regime 下 2000 labels 内永远达不到 crossover——variance explosion 太严重，16 或 64 个 cell 分不到足够 labels。这直接打击 \\\"as few as 250 expert labels\\\" 的 headline。只有 extreme regime + K=2 的 crossover 在 350 处，但 extreme regime 在 real data 上不存在（exp-003）。\\n\"\n606\t  },\n607\t  {\n608\t    \"name\": \"PPCI Baseline Comparison\",\n609\t    \"description\": \"PPCI (Sui et al., 2026) kernel-based conditional correction vs EC-HTE， covariate-side vs outcome-side error，composition 实验。\\n\",\n610\t    \"results\": {\n611\t      \"ppci_bias_on_covariate_error_setting\": 0.45,\n612\t      \"echte_bias_on_covariate_error_setting\": 0.08,\n613\t      \"ppci_bias_on_outcome_error_setting\": 0.05,\n614\t      \"echte_bias_on_outcome_error_setting\": 0.42,\n615\t      \"ppci_bias_on_both_errors\": 0.38,\n616\t      \"echte_bias_on_both_errors\": 0.35,\n617\t      \"composed_ppci_then_echte_bias\": 0.22,\n618\t      \"composed_echte_then_ppci_bias\": 0.25,\n619\t      \"ppci_partial_effectiveness_on_covariate_error\": 0.55\n620\t    },\n621\t    \"tables\": [\n622\t      {\n623\t        \"title\": \"Table 11: EC-HTE vs PPCI Head-to-Head\",\n624\t        \"columns\": [\n625\t          \"error_type\",\n626\t          \"metric\",\n627\t          \"ppci\",\n628\t          \"echte\",\n629\t          \"composed\",\n630\t          \"no_correction\"\n631\t        ],\n632\t        \"rows\": [\n633\t          [\n634\t            \"covariate-only\",\n635\t            \"max_subgroup_bias\",\n636\t            0.45,\n637\t            0.08,\n638\t            \"-\",\n639\t            1.0\n640\t          ],\n641\t          [\n642\t            \"outcome-only\",\n643\t            \"max_subgroup_bias\",\n644\t            0.05,\n645\t            0.42,\n646\t            \"-\",\n647\t            1.0\n648\t          ],\n649\t          [\n650\t            \"both\",\n651\t            \"max_subgroup_bias\",\n652\t            0.38,\n653\t            0.35,\n654\t            0.22,\n655\t            1.0\n656\t          ],\n657\t          [\n658\t            \"covariate-only\",\n659\t            \"coverage\",\n660\t            0.82,\n661\t            0.87,\n662\t            \"-\",\n663\t            0.72\n664\t          ],\n665\t          [\n666\t            \"outcome-only\",\n667\t            \"coverage\",\n668\t            0.91,\n669\t            0.78,\n670\t            \"-\",\n671\t            0.72\n672\t          ],\n673\t          [\n674\t            \"both\",\n675\t            \"coverage\",\n676\t            0.8,\n677\t            0.83,\n678\t            0.85,\n679\t            0.68\n680\t          ]\n681\t        ]\n682\t      }\n683\t    ],\n684\t    \"figures\": [],\n685\t    \"analysis\": \"PPCI 在 covariate-error 场景的 partial effectiveness（bias 降 55%）是 worst 档的关键 complication。论文不能说 \\\"PPCI 解决不了我们的问题\\\"，只能说 \\\"EC-HTE 在 covariate-error 上 更优（bias 0.08 vs 0.45），但 PPCI 也有效果\\\"。Composition 实验提供了一些 value-add（0.22 < min(0.38, 0.35)），可以作为 \\\"combined framework\\\" 的 positive result，但不是 dramatic。 建议在论文中诚实画出 overlap，用 \\\"complementary but partially overlapping\\\" framing。\\n\\n\\nPPCI 设计上处理 outcome-side measurement error，但 kernel localization 在 covariate-side error 上也有 partial effectiveness（bias 0.45 vs no-correction 的 ~1.0）。原因：PPCI 的 kernel 在 covariate space 做 local correction，当 covariate error 与 outcome error 相关时 （在 LLM annotation 中常见——同一个 LLM 标注 covariate 和 outcome），PPCI 间接 pick up 了 一些 covariate-side correction。这削弱了 EC-HTE 的 differentiation story——reviewer 会说 \\\"PPCI 已经部分解决了你的问题\\\"。Composition（先 EC-HTE 后 PPCI）有改善但不是 additive—— double correction 引入 over-adjustment。differentiation 不是 clean binary，而是 messy spectrum。\\n\"\n686\t  },\n687\t  {\n688\t    \"name\": \"Multi-LLM Annotator Comparison\",\n689\t    \"description\": \"GPT-4.1 vs Qwen3-235B vs Claude Sonnet 4.6，测量 misclassification heterogeneity 差异。 寻找触发显著 heterogeneity 的 LLM/domain 组合。\\n\",\n690\t    \"results\": {\n691\t      \"gpt4_max_min_ratio\": 1.12,\n692\t      \"qwen3_max_min_ratio\": 1.18,\n693\t      \"claude_sonnet_max_min_ratio\": 1.1,\n694\t      \"gpt4_ec_hte_benefit_bias_reduction_pct\": 22,\n695\t      \"qwen3_ec_hte_benefit_bias_reduction_pct\": 38,\n696\t      \"claude_sonnet_ec_hte_benefit_bias_reduction_pct\": 18,\n697\t      \"qwen3_specific_subgroup_with_high_error\": \"refugee_female_low_education\",\n698\t      \"qwen3_high_error_subgroup_accuracy\": 0.71,\n699\t      \"qwen3_low_error_subgroup_accuracy\": 0.89,\n700\t      \"qwen3_specific_case_bias_amplification\": 1.45,\n701\t      \"correlation_llm_quality_vs_heterogeneity\": -0.85\n702\t    },\n703\t    \"tables\": [\n704\t      {\n705\t        \"title\": \"Table 12: Cross-LLM Misclassification Heterogeneity\",\n706\t        \"columns\": [\n707\t          \"llm\",\n708\t          \"overall_acc\",\n709\t          \"max_min_ratio_k2\",\n710\t          \"max_min_ratio_k4\",\n711\t          \"ec_hte_benefit_pct\"\n712\t        ],\n713\t        \"rows\": [\n714\t          [\n715\t            \"GPT-4.1\",\n716\t            0.88,\n717\t            1.12,\n718\t            1.08,\n719\t            22\n720\t          ],\n721\t          [\n722\t            \"Qwen3-235B\",\n723\t            0.82,\n724\t            1.18,\n725\t            1.15,\n726\t            38\n727\t          ],\n728\t          [\n729\t            \"Claude Sonnet 4.6\",\n730\t            0.9,\n731\t            1.1,\n732\t            1.07,\n733\t            18\n734\t          ]\n735\t        ]\n736\t      },\n737\t      {\n738\t        \"title\": \"Table 13: Qwen3 Subgroup-Level Accuracy (Best Case for Heterogeneity)\",\n739\t        \"columns\": [\n740\t          \"subgroup\",\n741\t          \"n\",\n742\t          \"accuracy\",\n743\t          \"se\"\n744\t        ],\n745\t        \"rows\": [\n746\t          [\n747\t            \"refugee_female_low_edu\",\n748\t            85,\n749\t            0.71,\n750\t            0.049\n751\t          ],\n752\t          [\n753\t            \"refugee_female_high_edu\",\n754\t            120,\n755\t            0.8,\n756\t            0.037\n757\t          ],\n758\t          [\n759\t            \"refugee_male\",\n760\t            180,\n761\t            0.83,\n762\t            0.028\n763\t          ],\n764\t          [\n765\t            \"host_female\",\n766\t            165,\n767\t            0.87,\n768\t            0.026\n769\t          ],\n770\t          [\n771\t            \"host_male\",\n772\t            150,\n773\t            0.89,\n774\t            0.026\n775\t          ]\n776\t        ]\n777\t      }\n778\t    ],\n779\t    \"figures\": [],\n780\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-008 的 silver lining：Qwen3 × refugee_female_low_edu 是一个 genuine case study， 可以用来说 \\\"问题在特定 LLM/domain 组合下确实存在\\\"。但 sample size 太小（n=85）导致 accuracy SE 大（0.049），reviewer 可能质疑 heterogeneity 的 statistical significance。 negative correlation 发现是 double-edged：对 field 是好消息（LLM 越好问题越小）， 对论文是坏消息（motivation weakens over time）。建议在论文中用这个 case study 作为 \\\"illustrative example of when EC-HTE matters\\\"，同时诚实讨论 trend。\\n\\n\\nFrontier LLMs（GPT-4.1, Claude Sonnet）的 heterogeneity 低（ratio ~1.10–1.12），因为 这些模型在 political text 上广泛训练过，subgroup 间差异被高 capacity 压平。Qwen3 稍高 （1.18）但仍 modest。有趣的发现是 Qwen3 在 specific intersectional subgroup（refugee × female × low education，语言最复杂）上 accuracy 显著低（0.71 vs 平均 0.82），创造了一个 局部的 high heterogeneity case（max/min 在这对 subgroups 间可达 1.25）。但这只在 finest granularity 出现，overall K=2 或 K=4 水平上被平均掉。LLM quality vs heterogeneity 的 negative correlation（-0.85）暗示随着 LLM 进步问题会 further diminish。\\n\"\n781\t  },\n782\t  {\n783\t    \"name\": \"Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\",\n784\t    \"description\": \"CATE-weighted allocation vs uniform vs uncertainty-only，在 fixed expert budget 下 优化 subgroup CATE estimation precision。\\n\",\n785\t    \"results\": {\n786\t      \"adaptive_rmse_vs_uniform_reduction_pct_n250\": 12,\n787\t      \"adaptive_rmse_vs_uniform_reduction_pct_n500\": 8,\n788\t      \"adaptive_rmse_vs_uniform_reduction_pct_n1000\": 4,\n789\t      \"adaptive_vs_uncertainty_only_reduction_pct_n250\": 5,\n790\t      \"adaptive_coverage_n250\": 0.86,\n791\t      \"uniform_coverage_n250\": 0.84,\n792\t      \"optimal_allocation_concentration_gini\": 0.35,\n793\t      \"runtime_overhead_vs_uniform_pct\": 180\n794\t    },\n795\t    \"tables\": [\n796\t      {\n797\t        \"title\": \"Table 14: Adaptive Allocation Results\",\n798\t        \"columns\": [\n799\t          \"n_expert\",\n800\t          \"method\",\n801\t          \"rmse\",\n802\t          \"coverage\",\n803\t          \"runtime_sec\"\n804\t        ],\n805\t        \"rows\": [\n806\t          [\n807\t            250,\n808\t            \"uniform\",\n809\t            0.048,\n810\t            0.84,\n811\t            12\n812\t          ],\n813\t          [\n814\t            250,\n815\t            \"uncertainty_only\",\n816\t            0.045,\n817\t            0.85,\n818\t            28\n819\t          ],\n820\t          [\n821\t            250,\n822\t            \"cate_weighted\",\n823\t            0.042,\n824\t            0.86,\n825\t            34\n826\t          ],\n827\t          [\n828\t            500,\n829\t            \"uniform\",\n830\t            0.032,\n831\t            0.87,\n832\t            12\n833\t          ],\n834\t          [\n835\t            500,\n836\t            \"cate_weighted\",\n837\t            0.029,\n838\t            0.88,\n839\t            35\n840\t          ],\n841\t          [\n842\t            1000,\n843\t            \"uniform\",\n844\t            0.021,\n845\t            0.9,\n846\t            12\n847\t          ],\n848\t          [\n849\t            1000,\n850\t            \"cate_weighted\",\n851\t            0.02,\n852\t            0.9,\n853\t            36\n854\t          ]\n855\t        ]\n856\t      }\n857\t    ],\n858\t    \"figures\": [],\n859\t    \"analysis\": \"Adaptive allocation 不够 dramatic 作为 pivot target（Angle C 不可行除非效果更大）。 但 12% improvement at n=250 可以作为 \\\"practical tip\\\" 放在论文中，不需要是 main contribution。 建议保留在 appendix 作为 extension，不投入更多 effort。\\n\\n\\nAdaptive allocation 在 worst 档下有 moderate 效果。CATE-weighting 在 n=250 时带来 12% RMSE reduction vs uniform——这是因为即使 overall heterogeneity 不大，将 budget 集中在 high-CATE × high-error subgroups 仍然 reduces 最大 bottleneck。但 improvement 随 n 增大 快速衰减（n=1000 时仅 4%），因为 uniform allocation 在大 budget 下已经 adequate。 与 uncertainty-only allocation 相比优势更小（5%），因为在 worst 档下 CATE heterogeneity 和 error heterogeneity 的 correlation 弱——uncertainty-only 已经 capture 了大部分 signal。 Coverage 微弱改善。Runtime overhead 高（180%），因为需要 pilot estimates。 这不足以作为论文 pivot 的主贡献——improvement 太小且仅在 small n 显著。\\n\"\n860\t  },\n861\t  {\n862\t    \"name\": \"Robustness to Misspecified Subgroups\",\n863\t    \"description\": \"EC-HTE 在 subgroup structure noisy/overlapping 或与 true structure 不 aligned 时的表现。\\n\",\n864\t    \"results\": {\n865\t      \"echte_rmse_correct_subgroups\": 0.035,\n866\t      \"echte_rmse_noisy_subgroups_10pct_noise\": 0.038,\n867\t      \"echte_rmse_noisy_subgroups_30pct_noise\": 0.048,\n868\t      \"echte_rmse_misaligned_subgroups\": 0.055,\n869\t      \"global_rmse_misaligned_subgroups\": 0.042,\n870\t      \"echte_worse_than_global_at_noise_pct\": 25,\n871\t      \"hb_shrinkage_at_30pct_noise\": 0.72,\n872\t      \"hb_recovery_vs_mle_at_30pct_noise_pct\": 8\n873\t    },\n874\t    \"tables\": [\n875\t      {\n876\t        \"title\": \"Table 15: Robustness to Subgroup Misspecification\",\n877\t        \"columns\": [\n878\t          \"condition\",\n879\t          \"echte_hb_rmse\",\n880\t          \"echte_mle_rmse\",\n881\t          \"global_rmse\",\n882\t          \"echte_vs_global_pct\"\n883\t        ],\n884\t        \"rows\": [\n885\t          [\n886\t            \"correct subgroups\",\n887\t            0.035,\n888\t            0.036,\n889\t            0.04,\n890\t            \"-12.5%\"\n891\t          ],\n892\t          [\n893\t            \"10% noise\",\n894\t            0.038,\n895\t            0.04,\n896\t            0.04,\n897\t            \"-5.0%\"\n898\t          ],\n899\t          [\n900\t            \"20% noise\",\n901\t            0.042,\n902\t            0.046,\n903\t            0.04,\n904\t            \"+5.0%\"\n905\t          ],\n906\t          [\n907\t            \"30% noise\",\n908\t            0.048,\n909\t            0.054,\n910\t            0.04,\n911\t            \"+20.0%\"\n912\t          ],\n913\t          [\n914\t            \"misaligned subgroups\",\n915\t            0.055,\n916\t            0.062,\n917\t            0.042,\n918\t            \"+31.0%\"\n919\t          ]\n920\t        ]\n921\t      }\n922\t    ],\n923\t    \"figures\": [],\n924\t    \"analysis\": \"Robustness 结果对 worst 档有 mixed implications。Negative：EC-HTE 不是 \\\"never worse than global\\\"——在 misspecified subgroups 下可以更差。Positive：HB partial pooling 的 adaptive shrinkage 确实在 work，只是不够 fully salvage。论文必须讨论这个 limitation 并建议 practitioners 用 diagnostic criterion + domain knowledge 验证 subgroup choice。 这也 weakens Claim 2 的 \\\"applicable to any CATE estimator\\\" 部分——需要加 caveat。\\n\\n\\nSubgroup misspecification 对 EC-HTE 的打击比对 global 更大——因为 EC-HTE 依赖 subgroup structure 来 estimate per-group confusion matrices，而 global 对 subgroup 定义 robust by construction。在 10% noise 下降幅小（8%），但 30% noise 下 EC-HTE RMSE 增加 37%， 且在 25% noise 处 EC-HTE 反转为 worse than global。Misaligned subgroups（true heterogeneity 沿 dimension A，correction 沿 dimension B）更严重——EC-HTE 比 global 差 31%。HB partial pooling 在高 noise 下确实 shrink toward global（shrinkage 0.72），部分 mitigate 了问题 （比 MLE stratified 好 8%），但不够 fully recover。这暴露了 EC-HTE 的 Achilles heel： 需要 correct subgroup specification，而在实践中这可能需要 domain expertise。\\n\"\n925\t  },\n926\t  {\n927\t    \"name\": \"Causal Forest Integration\",\n928\t    \"description\": \"EC-HTE post-hoc correction on CausalForestDML leaf-level estimates， vs naive forest vs globally-corrected forest。\\n\",\n929\t    \"results\": {\n930\t      \"echte_forest_rmse\": 0.038,\n931\t      \"global_forest_rmse\": 0.036,\n932\t      \"naive_forest_rmse\": 0.045,\n933\t      \"echte_forest_coverage\": 0.85,\n934\t      \"global_forest_coverage\": 0.83,\n935\t      \"naive_forest_coverage\": 0.75,\n936\t      \"echte_forest_vs_global_improvement_pct\": -5.6,\n937\t      \"variance_adjusted_ci_width_ratio\": 1.35,\n938\t      \"leaf_level_correction_convergence_rate\": 0.78\n939\t    },\n940\t    \"tables\": [\n941\t      {\n942\t        \"title\": \"Table 16: Causal Forest Integration Results\",\n943\t        \"columns\": [\n944\t          \"method\",\n945\t          \"rmse\",\n946\t          \"bias\",\n947\t          \"coverage\",\n948\t          \"ci_width_mean\",\n949\t          \"convergence_rate\"\n950\t        ],\n951\t        \"rows\": [\n952\t          [\n953\t            \"Naive Forest\",\n954\t            0.045,\n955\t            0.032,\n956\t            0.75,\n957\t            0.08,\n958\t            1.0\n959\t          ],\n960\t          [\n961\t            \"Global-Corrected Forest\",\n962\t            0.036,\n963\t            0.018,\n964\t            0.83,\n965\t            0.1,\n966\t            1.0\n967\t          ],\n968\t          [\n969\t            \"EC-HTE Forest (leaf-level)\",\n970\t            0.038,\n971\t            0.012,\n972\t            0.85,\n973\t            0.135,\n974\t            0.78\n975\t          ],\n976\t          [\n977\t            \"EC-HTE Forest (subgroup-level)\",\n978\t            0.037,\n979\t            0.015,\n980\t            0.84,\n981\t            0.12,\n982\t            0.95\n983\t          ]\n984\t        ]\n985\t      }\n986\t    ],\n987\t    \"figures\": [],\n988\t    \"analysis\": \"Causal forest integration 不是可行的 pivot direction（Angle C fails for exp-011）。 Leaf-level correction 的 variance-bias tradeoff 不利，convergence issues 更是 red flag。 Subgroup-level correction applied to forest（而非 leaf-level）表现稍好（RMSE 0.037 vs 0.036）， 接近 global 但没有 clear win。建议在论文中不把 forest integration 作为 contribution， 仅在 discussion 中提到 \\\"straightforward extension exists but requires careful variance management\\\"。\\n\\nCausal forest integration 在 worst 档下表现差于 global correction。原因：forest 的 leaf 已经是数据驱动的 subgroups，与手工定义的 correction subgroups 不 aligned。Leaf-level correction 每个 leaf 的 sample size 太小（典型 50–200 observations），confusion matrix 估计 noisy，variance inflation（CI width +35%）抵消了 bias reduction。Global correction 在 forest setting 下更 robust——forest 自身的 adaptive partitioning 已经 partially account for heterogeneity。EC-HTE 的 RMSE 反而比 global 高 5.6%。收敛率只有 78%（22% 的 MC runs 中 leaf-level correction 的 matrix inversion 出现 numerical issues）。 这意味着 Claim 2 的 \\\"causal forest integration\\\" 部分在 worst 档下 fails。\\n\"\n989\t  }\n990\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37075016-2431-4308-9c0a-0827a1b2a63c","uuid":"03b2bdd9-cb71-4b72-8bfa-ba19b9f9f579","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:11:17.699Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T194535/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"HB EC-HTE Synthetic Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"HB Dirichlet partial pooling vs MLE/Laplace stratified correction， full regime sweep (extreme/moderate/homogeneous × n_expert 100–2000 × K=2,4)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"hb_rmse_vs_mle_extreme_k2_n250\": -0.02,\n      \"hb_rmse_vs_mle_extreme_k2_n1000\": -0.01,\n      \"hb_rmse_vs_mle_moderate_k2_n250\": 0.0,\n      \"hb_rmse_vs_mle_moderate_k4_n250\": 0.03,\n      \"hb_rmse_vs_mle_homogeneous_k2_n250\": 0.01,\n      \"hb_coverage_95ci_extreme_k2_n250\": 0.86,\n      \"hb_coverage_95ci_extreme_k2_n1000\": 0.91,\n      \"hb_coverage_95ci_moderate_k2_n250\": 0.84,\n      \"hb_coverage_95ci_moderate_k4_n250\": 0.83,\n      \"hb_coverage_95ci_homogeneous_k2_n250\": 0.88,\n      \"mle_coverage_95ci_extreme_k2_n250\": 0.82,\n      \"mle_coverage_95ci_moderate_k4_n250\": 0.79,\n      \"partial_pooling_shrinkage_factor_moderate_k4\": 0.65,\n      \"mcmc_rhat_max\": 1.003,\n      \"mcmc_ess_min\": 280,\n      \"mcmc_runtime_vs_mle_ratio\": 45.0,\n      \"mc_runs\": 1000\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 1: HB vs MLE Stratified — RMSE and Coverage by Regime\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"regime\",\n          \"K\",\n          \"n_expert\",\n          \"rmse_hb\",\n          \"rmse_mle\",\n          \"rmse_diff_pct\",\n          \"coverage_hb\",\n          \"coverage_mle\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"extreme\",\n            2,\n            250,\n            0.041,\n            0.042,\n            \"-2.4%\",\n            0.86,\n            0.82\n          ],\n          [\n            \"extreme\",\n            2,\n            1000,\n            0.022,\n            0.022,\n            \"-1.0%\",\n            0.91,\n            0.89\n          ],\n          [\n            \"extreme\",\n            4,\n            250,\n            0.058,\n            0.055,\n            \"+5.5%\",\n            0.83,\n            0.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"moderate\",\n            2,\n            250,\n            0.035,\n            0.035,\n            \"0.0%\",\n            0.84,\n            0.83\n          ],\n          [\n            \"moderate\",\n            2,\n            1000,\n            0.019,\n            0.019,\n            \"0.0%\",\n            0.9,\n            0.89\n          ],\n          [\n            \"moderate\",\n            4,\n            250,\n            0.049,\n            0.048,\n            \"+2.1%\",\n            0.83,\n            0.79\n          ],\n          [\n            \"homogeneous\",\n            2,\n            250,\n            0.03,\n            0.03,\n            \"+1.0%\",\n            0.88,\n            0.87\n          ],\n          [\n            \"homogeneous\",\n            4,\n            250,\n            0.038,\n            0.037,\n            \"+2.7%\",\n            0.85,\n            0.84\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 2: MCMC Diagnostics Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"parameter_group\",\n          \"rhat_median\",\n          \"rhat_max\",\n          \"ess_bulk_min\",\n          \"ess_tail_min\",\n          \"runtime_sec\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"confusion_matrix_k2\",\n            1.001,\n            1.003,\n            450,\n            280,\n            42\n          ],\n          [\n            \"confusion_matrix_k4\",\n            1.002,\n            1.005,\n            320,\n            210,\n            185\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cate_posterior_k2\",\n            1.001,\n            1.002,\n            520,\n            310,\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cate_posterior_k4\",\n            1.002,\n            1.004,\n            380,\n            240,\n            \"-\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"HB partial pooling 在 worst 档下不是 selling point。extreme regime 的微弱优势无法外推到 realistic 数据。Coverage 偏低是结构性问题——需要 bootstrap 或 sandwich variance 补救， 但这会进一步增加计算成本。论文中应诚实报告 HB 的边际价值有限，将贡献重心转向 bias mechanism 的 characterization 而非 estimation method。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档下 HB 与 MLE stratified 差异不显著。原因：partial pooling 的价值在于 borrowing strength across subgroups，但当 heterogeneity 本身不大时，MLE stratified 估计已经足够准确，Dirichlet prior 的 shrinkage 几乎无事可做。在 extreme regime（人造的 5x+ heterogeneity）下 HB 略优（RMSE 降 2%）， 但这个 regime 在 realistic 数据上不出现。moderate regime 下差异 < 1%。K=4 时 HB 反而略差（+3%）， 因为 Dirichlet 的 4×4 confusion matrix 参数空间更大，prior 选择更敏感，且 n_expert=250 时 每 cell 样本不足。Coverage 系统性偏低（83–88%），源于 confusion matrix 估计的 sampling uncertainty 未被充分传播到 CATE CI 中——posterior predictive intervals 低估了矩阵逆运算 中的 error propagation。MCMC 收敛良好但 runtime 是 MLE 的 45 倍，reviewer 会质疑实用性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Formal Bias Bound Verification\",\n    \"description\": \"解析推导 bias = f(Δπ, Δτ)，K=2 和 K>2 两种情况。 MC 验证 analytic prediction vs empirical bias 的 R²。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"analytic_r_squared_k2\": 0.92,\n      \"analytic_r_squared_k4\": 0.68,\n      \"analytic_r_squared_k8\": 0.52,\n      \"bound_tightness_ratio_k2\": 1.15,\n      \"bound_tightness_ratio_k4\": 2.3,\n      \"bound_tightness_ratio_k8\": 3.8,\n      \"bias_amplification_at_realistic_delta_pi_0p05\": 1.08,\n      \"bias_amplification_at_realistic_delta_pi_0p10\": 1.18,\n      \"bias_amplification_at_realistic_delta_pi_0p20\": 1.45,\n      \"bias_amplification_at_extreme_delta_pi_0p40\": 3.2,\n      \"debiasing_hurts_threshold_delta_pi\": 0.08,\n      \"mc_ci_width_bias_estimate\": 0.003\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 3: Analytic Bound Accuracy by K\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"r_squared\",\n          \"bound_tightness_ratio\",\n          \"n_mc_runs\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            0.92,\n            1.15,\n            1000\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.68,\n            2.3,\n            1000\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            0.52,\n            3.8,\n            500\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 4: Bias Amplification (Global/No-Correction) by Δπ\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"delta_pi\",\n          \"delta_tau\",\n          \"bias_amplification_k2\",\n          \"bias_amplification_k4\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0.05,\n            0.3,\n            1.08,\n            1.12\n          ],\n          [\n            0.1,\n            0.3,\n            1.18,\n            1.25\n          ],\n          [\n            0.2,\n            0.3,\n            1.45,\n            1.62\n          ],\n          [\n            0.4,\n            0.3,\n            3.2,\n            4.1\n          ],\n          [\n            0.05,\n            0.6,\n            1.15,\n            1.2\n          ],\n          [\n            0.1,\n            0.6,\n            1.35,\n            1.48\n          ],\n          [\n            0.2,\n            0.6,\n            2.1,\n            2.55\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Δπ×Δτ bound 在 K=2 时优雅且 tight，但 generalization 到 K>2 失败——这是 worst 档的 核心问题。论文不能宣称 \\\"通用诊断准则\\\"，只能说 \\\"K=2 的 exact characterization + K>2 的 conservative sufficient condition\\\"。Realistic parameter 区间内 bias amplification 太小， \\\"debiasing can hurt by 5–10x\\\" 的 headline 只在人造 extreme regime 成立。需要 reframe： \\\"我们证明了在何种条件下问题才会严重，并发现当前 LLM 通常不触发这些条件。\\\"\\n\\n\\nK=2 时 Δπ×Δτ 形式是 exact（R²=0.92，残差来自 finite-sample noise），因为二分类 confusion matrix 只有一个自由度，bias 表达式可以 closed-form 展开。但 K>2 时 confusion matrix 是 K×K，交叉项爆炸——K=4 有 12 个 off-diagonal 元素，Δπ×Δτ 的简单乘积形式只是 first-order approximation，忽略了 cross-subgroup misclassification 的高阶交互。R² 从 0.92（K=2） 降到 0.68（K=4）再到 0.52（K=8），bound 变得越来越松（tightness ratio 从 1.15 到 3.8）。 在 realistic Δπ 范围（0.05–0.10，对应 LLM 在不同 subgroup 间 5–10pp 的 accuracy 差异）， bias amplification 仅 1.08–1.18x，不构成实际危害。只有在 Δπ≥0.20 时才开始显著（1.45x）， 而这个水平在当前 LLM 上很少见。\\\"Debiasing can hurt\\\" 的 threshold 虽然存在（Δπ≈0.08）， 但 hurt 的程度很小。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Semi-Synthetic Benchmark\",\n    \"description\": \"Real tweet corpus + injected CATE structure + GPT-4.1/Qwen3-235B 标注。 测量 real misclassification heterogeneity，EC-HTE vs global vs no-correction。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4_misclass_heterogeneity_max_min_ratio\": 1.12,\n      \"qwen3_misclass_heterogeneity_max_min_ratio\": 1.18,\n      \"gpt4_overall_accuracy\": 0.88,\n      \"qwen3_overall_accuracy\": 0.82,\n      \"ec_hte_subgroup_bias_reduction_vs_global_gpt4\": 0.25,\n      \"ec_hte_subgroup_bias_reduction_vs_global_qwen3\": 0.4,\n      \"global_vs_nocorrection_bias_amplification_gpt4\": 1.05,\n      \"global_vs_nocorrection_bias_amplification_qwen3\": 1.12,\n      \"ec_hte_coverage_95ci_gpt4\": 0.87,\n      \"ec_hte_coverage_95ci_qwen3\": 0.85,\n      \"global_coverage_95ci_gpt4\": 0.85,\n      \"global_coverage_95ci_qwen3\": 0.82,\n      \"nocorrection_coverage_95ci_gpt4\": 0.78,\n      \"nocorrection_coverage_95ci_qwen3\": 0.74,\n      \"max_subgroup_bias_global_gpt4\": 0.015,\n      \"max_subgroup_bias_global_qwen3\": 0.028,\n      \"max_subgroup_bias_echte_gpt4\": 0.011,\n      \"max_subgroup_bias_echte_qwen3\": 0.017\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 5: Misclassification Heterogeneity — Real LLM on Semi-Synthetic Data\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"llm\",\n          \"overall_acc\",\n          \"subgroup_acc_min\",\n          \"subgroup_acc_max\",\n          \"max_min_ratio\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4.1\",\n            0.88,\n            0.86,\n            0.9,\n            1.12\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-235B\",\n            0.82,\n            0.78,\n            0.86,\n            1.18\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 6: Subgroup CATE Bias (Max Across Subgroups)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"gpt4_max_bias\",\n          \"gpt4_mean_bias\",\n          \"qwen3_max_bias\",\n          \"qwen3_mean_bias\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"No Correction\",\n            0.025,\n            0.018,\n            0.042,\n            0.03\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Global Correction\",\n            0.015,\n            0.01,\n            0.028,\n            0.019\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EC-HTE (MLE)\",\n            0.012,\n            0.008,\n            0.018,\n            0.012\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EC-HTE (HB)\",\n            0.011,\n            0.008,\n            0.017,\n            0.011\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Semi-synthetic 结果是 worst 档叙事的核心证据：real LLM 的 misclassification heterogeneity 不足以让 global correction 失效。EC-HTE 有微弱优势但 \\\"insurance, not necessity\\\"。 论文 framing 必须转向 Angle A：\\\"好消息是当前 LLM 通常不触发这个问题\\\"。 Qwen3 比 GPT-4.1 heterogeneity 略大，暗示 weaker LLMs 可能在某些 domain 触发—— 这为 exp-008 寻找 stronger case 提供方向。\\n\\n\\nReal LLM 数据上 misclassification heterogeneity 远低于 synthetic extreme regime。 GPT-4.1 accuracy 高（88%）且跨 subgroup 差异小（max/min ratio 1.12），因为 frontier LLM 在 political text 分类上已经足够好，不同 subgroup 的语言难度差异被模型能力压平。Qwen3 稍差 （82%, ratio 1.18），但仍远低于 \\\"5x\\\" 的 extreme 设定。结果：global correction 几乎不 hurt （amplification 1.05–1.12x），EC-HTE 的 bias reduction 有但幅度小（25–40%），绝对 bias 差异在 0.004–0.011 之间——统计上可能显著但实际上微不足道。Coverage 偏低延续了 exp-001 的 pattern。这个结果直接动摇 Claim 1 的 \\\"practically consequential\\\" 部分。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Ashwin et al. Real-Data Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Rohingya refugee interview 数据，LLM 标注 error 与 refugee status/gender/education 相关。 EC-HTE vs global correction on real CATEs。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"misclass_heterogeneity_max_min_ratio\": 1.22,\n      \"ec_hte_cate_shift_vs_global_max_subgroup\": 0.035,\n      \"ec_hte_cate_shift_vs_global_mean\": 0.018,\n      \"ec_hte_coverage\": 0.86,\n      \"global_coverage\": 0.83,\n      \"nocorrection_coverage\": 0.76,\n      \"bias_amplification_global_vs_nocorrection\": 1.15,\n      \"qualitative_conclusion_changes\": 0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 7: Ashwin et al. — Misclassification by Subgroup\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"subgroup\",\n          \"n\",\n          \"llm_accuracy\",\n          \"accuracy_se\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"female_refugee\",\n            420,\n            0.78,\n            0.02\n          ],\n          [\n            \"male_refugee\",\n            380,\n            0.82,\n            0.02\n          ],\n          [\n            \"female_host\",\n            350,\n            0.88,\n            0.017\n          ],\n          [\n            \"male_host\",\n            310,\n            0.9,\n            0.017\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 8: CATE Estimates by Method\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"subgroup\",\n          \"cate_nocorr\",\n          \"cate_global\",\n          \"cate_echte\",\n          \"shift_global_to_echte\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"female_refugee\",\n            0.142,\n            0.158,\n            0.172,\n            0.014\n          ],\n          [\n            \"male_refugee\",\n            0.118,\n            0.131,\n            0.138,\n            0.007\n          ],\n          [\n            \"female_host\",\n            0.085,\n            0.094,\n            0.09,\n            -0.004\n          ],\n          [\n            \"male_host\",\n            0.062,\n            0.069,\n            0.065,\n            -0.004\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Real data 上 EC-HTE 有方向性的 correction 但幅度不足以改变结论。没有 ground truth 是致命 弱点——无法证明 EC-HTE 更接近 truth 还是引入了 overcorrection。论文只能定性地论证 \\\"stratified correction 的方向与 known error patterns 一致\\\"。作为 supporting evidence 可以放在论文中，但不能作为 standalone claim 的证据。\\n\\n\\nAshwin et al. 数据的优势是 known demographic-correlated error，但 refugee interview text 的 LLM 分类难度差异（按 refugee status/gender）可能只是 moderate。max/min ratio 1.22 比 semi-synthetic 高一些（因为 code-switching、方言、文化特定表达确实影响 LLM），但仍不到 dramatic 的程度。EC-HTE 的 CATE 调整量（0.035）虽然比 semi-synthetic 大，但没有改变任何 subgroup 的 qualitative conclusion（即哪个 subgroup 的 treatment effect 更大的排序不变）。 这意味着 EC-HTE 在实际决策层面没有 impact。Coverage 稍好于 semi-synthetic 但仍低于 nominal。 无 ground truth CATE 导致无法计算 bias——只能报告 \\\"correction shift\\\"，reviewer 可能质疑 这是 improvement 还是 overcorrection。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Diagnostic Criterion Validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Δπ×Δτ product 作为 diagnostic，ROC 分析预测 \\\"global correction harmful\\\" 的准确性。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"diagnostic_auc_k2\": 0.74,\n      \"diagnostic_auc_k4\": 0.65,\n      \"diagnostic_auc_overall\": 0.7,\n      \"optimal_threshold_delta_pi_times_delta_tau\": 0.025,\n      \"sensitivity_at_fpr_0p10\": 0.52,\n      \"specificity_at_tpr_0p90\": 0.35,\n      \"fraction_settings_where_global_harmful\": 0.18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 9: Diagnostic ROC Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"setting\",\n          \"auc\",\n          \"sensitivity_at_fpr10\",\n          \"specificity_at_tpr90\",\n          \"n_settings\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"K=2 synthetic\",\n            0.74,\n            0.58,\n            0.42,\n            500\n          ],\n          [\n            \"K=4 synthetic\",\n            0.65,\n            0.45,\n            0.28,\n            500\n          ],\n          [\n            \"semi-synthetic (GPT-4.1)\",\n            0.71,\n            0.5,\n            0.33,\n            100\n          ],\n          [\n            \"semi-synthetic (Qwen3)\",\n            0.73,\n            0.55,\n            0.38,\n            100\n          ],\n          [\n            \"overall\",\n            0.7,\n            0.52,\n            0.35,\n            1200\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"AUC < 0.75 意味着 Claim 3（diagnostic criterion）作为 standalone contribution 失败。 不能推荐给 practitioners 说 \\\"用这个判断是否需要 stratified correction\\\"。但问题的 formalization 本身仍有价值——\\\"什么情况下应该担心\\\" 的问题此前无人提出。论文中 reframe 为 \\\"we provide a conservative sufficient condition, not a precise diagnostic\\\"：如果 Δπ×Δτ > threshold， 一定要用 stratified；如果 < threshold，大概率 safe 但不保证。这在 Angle A 叙事下 work。\\n\\n\\nDiagnostic AUC 受限于两个因素。(1) \\\"Global correction harmful\\\" 的 base rate 低（仅 18% 的 settings 触发），因为 realistic parameter 空间中 Δπ 和 Δτ 都倾向于小值——大多数时候 global correction 是 fine 的。低 base rate 让 classifier 难以 distinguish。(2) K>2 时 Δπ×Δτ 本身就不是好的 summary statistic（exp-002 已证明），sum-of-products 形式有 information loss。AUC=0.70 意味着 diagnostic 比随机好但远不够 reliable——sensitivity 和 specificity 无法同时高。作为 \\\"practical tool\\\" 推荐给用户是勉强的。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\",\n    \"description\": \"n_expert sweep {50, 100, 250, 500, 1000, 2000} × K ∈ {2, 4, 8}， 找 EC-HTE > Global 的 crossover point。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"crossover_n_k2_moderate\": 750,\n      \"crossover_n_k4_moderate\": \"never (within 2000)\",\n      \"crossover_n_k2_extreme\": 350,\n      \"crossover_n_k8_moderate\": \"never (within 2000)\",\n      \"hb_advantage_at_n250_k2_moderate_rmse_pct\": -1.5,\n      \"hb_advantage_at_n250_k4_moderate_rmse_pct\": 4.0,\n      \"hb_advantage_at_n1000_k2_moderate_rmse_pct\": -0.5,\n      \"ec_hte_rmse_at_n50_k2\": 0.095,\n      \"ec_hte_rmse_at_n100_k2\": 0.068,\n      \"ec_hte_rmse_at_n2000_k2\": 0.018,\n      \"global_rmse_at_n50_k2\": 0.052,\n      \"global_rmse_at_n2000_k2\": 0.019\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 10: Budget Crossover Analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"K\",\n          \"regime\",\n          \"crossover_n\",\n          \"ec_hte_rmse_at_crossover\",\n          \"global_rmse_at_crossover\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            2,\n            \"extreme\",\n            350,\n            0.032,\n            0.032\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"moderate\",\n            750,\n            0.024,\n            0.024\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            \"homogeneous\",\n            \">2000\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"extreme\",\n            650,\n            0.045,\n            0.045\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            \"moderate\",\n            \">2000\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"-\"\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            \"extreme\",\n            1200,\n            0.068,\n            0.068\n          ],\n          [\n            8,\n            \"moderate\",\n            \">2000\",\n            \"-\",\n            \"-\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Budget sensitivity 是 worst 档的另一个 pain point。EC-HTE 在 realistic settings 下需要 大量 expert labels 才能 justify——这与 \\\"reduce expert labeling burden\\\" 的叙事矛盾。 论文需要诚实报告：EC-HTE 是 insurance policy，只在高 heterogeneity 时 pay off， 且 cost 随 K 快速增长。建议将 K=2 作为主结果，K≥4 放 appendix 并讨论 limitations。\\n\\n\\nCrossover point 高（500–1000 range）因为 EC-HTE 需要足够 per-subgroup expert labels 来 估计 K×K confusion matrix——K=2 时每个 cell 需要 ~50 个 labels 才 stable，意味着总共需要 ~200+。但在 moderate heterogeneity 下 global 的 bias 很小，EC-HTE 的 variance cost（来自 subgroup-level estimation）直到 n=750 才被 bias reduction 补偿。K=4 和 K=8 在 moderate regime 下 2000 labels 内永远达不到 crossover——variance explosion 太严重，16 或 64 个 cell 分不到足够 labels。这直接打击 \\\"as few as 250 expert labels\\\" 的 headline。只有 extreme regime + K=2 的 crossover 在 350 处，但 extreme regime 在 real data 上不存在（exp-003）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"PPCI Baseline Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"PPCI (Sui et al., 2026) kernel-based conditional correction vs EC-HTE， covariate-side vs outcome-side error，composition 实验。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ppci_bias_on_covariate_error_setting\": 0.45,\n      \"echte_bias_on_covariate_error_setting\": 0.08,\n      \"ppci_bias_on_outcome_error_setting\": 0.05,\n      \"echte_bias_on_outcome_error_setting\": 0.42,\n      \"ppci_bias_on_both_errors\": 0.38,\n      \"echte_bias_on_both_errors\": 0.35,\n      \"composed_ppci_then_echte_bias\": 0.22,\n      \"composed_echte_then_ppci_bias\": 0.25,\n      \"ppci_partial_effectiveness_on_covariate_error\": 0.55\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 11: EC-HTE vs PPCI Head-to-Head\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"error_type\",\n          \"metric\",\n          \"ppci\",\n          \"echte\",\n          \"composed\",\n          \"no_correction\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"covariate-only\",\n            \"max_subgroup_bias\",\n            0.45,\n            0.08,\n            \"-\",\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"outcome-only\",\n            \"max_subgroup_bias\",\n            0.05,\n            0.42,\n            \"-\",\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"both\",\n            \"max_subgroup_bias\",\n            0.38,\n            0.35,\n            0.22,\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"covariate-only\",\n            \"coverage\",\n            0.82,\n            0.87,\n            \"-\",\n            0.72\n          ],\n          [\n            \"outcome-only\",\n            \"coverage\",\n            0.91,\n            0.78,\n            \"-\",\n            0.72\n          ],\n          [\n            \"both\",\n            \"coverage\",\n            0.8,\n            0.83,\n            0.85,\n            0.68\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"PPCI 在 covariate-error 场景的 partial effectiveness（bias 降 55%）是 worst 档的关键 complication。论文不能说 \\\"PPCI 解决不了我们的问题\\\"，只能说 \\\"EC-HTE 在 covariate-error 上 更优（bias 0.08 vs 0.45），但 PPCI 也有效果\\\"。Composition 实验提供了一些 value-add（0.22 < min(0.38, 0.35)），可以作为 \\\"combined framework\\\" 的 positive result，但不是 dramatic。 建议在论文中诚实画出 overlap，用 \\\"complementary but partially overlapping\\\" framing。\\n\\n\\nPPCI 设计上处理 outcome-side measurement error，但 kernel localization 在 covariate-side error 上也有 partial effectiveness（bias 0.45 vs no-correction 的 ~1.0）。原因：PPCI 的 kernel 在 covariate space 做 local correction，当 covariate error 与 outcome error 相关时 （在 LLM annotation 中常见——同一个 LLM 标注 covariate 和 outcome），PPCI 间接 pick up 了 一些 covariate-side correction。这削弱了 EC-HTE 的 differentiation story——reviewer 会说 \\\"PPCI 已经部分解决了你的问题\\\"。Composition（先 EC-HTE 后 PPCI）有改善但不是 additive—— double correction 引入 over-adjustment。differentiation 不是 clean binary，而是 messy spectrum。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Multi-LLM Annotator Comparison\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-4.1 vs Qwen3-235B vs Claude Sonnet 4.6，测量 misclassification heterogeneity 差异。 寻找触发显著 heterogeneity 的 LLM/domain 组合。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt4_max_min_ratio\": 1.12,\n      \"qwen3_max_min_ratio\": 1.18,\n      \"claude_sonnet_max_min_ratio\": 1.1,\n      \"gpt4_ec_hte_benefit_bias_reduction_pct\": 22,\n      \"qwen3_ec_hte_benefit_bias_reduction_pct\": 38,\n      \"claude_sonnet_ec_hte_benefit_bias_reduction_pct\": 18,\n      \"qwen3_specific_subgroup_with_high_error\": \"refugee_female_low_education\",\n      \"qwen3_high_error_subgroup_accuracy\": 0.71,\n      \"qwen3_low_error_subgroup_accuracy\": 0.89,\n      \"qwen3_specific_case_bias_amplification\": 1.45,\n      \"correlation_llm_quality_vs_heterogeneity\": -0.85\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 12: Cross-LLM Misclassification Heterogeneity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"llm\",\n          \"overall_acc\",\n          \"max_min_ratio_k2\",\n          \"max_min_ratio_k4\",\n          \"ec_hte_benefit_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"GPT-4.1\",\n            0.88,\n            1.12,\n            1.08,\n            22\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen3-235B\",\n            0.82,\n            1.18,\n            1.15,\n            38\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Claude Sonnet 4.6\",\n            0.9,\n            1.1,\n            1.07,\n            18\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 13: Qwen3 Subgroup-Level Accuracy (Best Case for Heterogeneity)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"subgroup\",\n          \"n\",\n          \"accuracy\",\n          \"se\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"refugee_female_low_edu\",\n            85,\n            0.71,\n            0.049\n          ],\n          [\n            \"refugee_female_high_edu\",\n            120,\n            0.8,\n            0.037\n          ],\n          [\n            \"refugee_male\",\n            180,\n            0.83,\n            0.028\n          ],\n          [\n            \"host_female\",\n            165,\n            0.87,\n            0.026\n          ],\n          [\n            \"host_male\",\n            150,\n            0.89,\n            0.026\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-008 的 silver lining：Qwen3 × refugee_female_low_edu 是一个 genuine case study， 可以用来说 \\\"问题在特定 LLM/domain 组合下确实存在\\\"。但 sample size 太小（n=85）导致 accuracy SE 大（0.049），reviewer 可能质疑 heterogeneity 的 statistical significance。 negative correlation 发现是 double-edged：对 field 是好消息（LLM 越好问题越小）， 对论文是坏消息（motivation weakens over time）。建议在论文中用这个 case study 作为 \\\"illustrative example of when EC-HTE matters\\\"，同时诚实讨论 trend。\\n\\n\\nFrontier LLMs（GPT-4.1, Claude Sonnet）的 heterogeneity 低（ratio ~1.10–1.12），因为 这些模型在 political text 上广泛训练过，subgroup 间差异被高 capacity 压平。Qwen3 稍高 （1.18）但仍 modest。有趣的发现是 Qwen3 在 specific intersectional subgroup（refugee × female × low education，语言最复杂）上 accuracy 显著低（0.71 vs 平均 0.82），创造了一个 局部的 high heterogeneity case（max/min 在这对 subgroups 间可达 1.25）。但这只在 finest granularity 出现，overall K=2 或 K=4 水平上被平均掉。LLM quality vs heterogeneity 的 negative correlation（-0.85）暗示随着 LLM 进步问题会 further diminish。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\",\n    \"description\": \"CATE-weighted allocation vs uniform vs uncertainty-only，在 fixed expert budget 下 优化 subgroup CATE estimation precision。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"adaptive_rmse_vs_uniform_reduction_pct_n250\": 12,\n      \"adaptive_rmse_vs_uniform_reduction_pct_n500\": 8,\n      \"adaptive_rmse_vs_uniform_reduction_pct_n1000\": 4,\n      \"adaptive_vs_uncertainty_only_reduction_pct_n250\": 5,\n      \"adaptive_coverage_n250\": 0.86,\n      \"uniform_coverage_n250\": 0.84,\n      \"optimal_allocation_concentration_gini\": 0.35,\n      \"runtime_overhead_vs_uniform_pct\": 180\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 14: Adaptive Allocation Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n_expert\",\n          \"method\",\n          \"rmse\",\n          \"coverage\",\n          \"runtime_sec\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            250,\n            \"uniform\",\n            0.048,\n            0.84,\n            12\n          ],\n          [\n            250,\n            \"uncertainty_only\",\n            0.045,\n            0.85,\n            28\n          ],\n          [\n            250,\n            \"cate_weighted\",\n            0.042,\n            0.86,\n            34\n          ],\n          [\n            500,\n            \"uniform\",\n            0.032,\n            0.87,\n            12\n          ],\n          [\n            500,\n            \"cate_weighted\",\n            0.029,\n            0.88,\n            35\n          ],\n          [\n            1000,\n            \"uniform\",\n            0.021,\n            0.9,\n            12\n          ],\n          [\n            1000,\n            \"cate_weighted\",\n            0.02,\n            0.9,\n            36\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Adaptive allocation 不够 dramatic 作为 pivot target（Angle C 不可行除非效果更大）。 但 12% improvement at n=250 可以作为 \\\"practical tip\\\" 放在论文中，不需要是 main contribution。 建议保留在 appendix 作为 extension，不投入更多 effort。\\n\\n\\nAdaptive allocation 在 worst 档下有 moderate 效果。CATE-weighting 在 n=250 时带来 12% RMSE reduction vs uniform——这是因为即使 overall heterogeneity 不大，将 budget 集中在 high-CATE × high-error subgroups 仍然 reduces 最大 bottleneck。但 improvement 随 n 增大 快速衰减（n=1000 时仅 4%），因为 uniform allocation 在大 budget 下已经 adequate。 与 uncertainty-only allocation 相比优势更小（5%），因为在 worst 档下 CATE heterogeneity 和 error heterogeneity 的 correlation 弱——uncertainty-only 已经 capture 了大部分 signal。 Coverage 微弱改善。Runtime overhead 高（180%），因为需要 pilot estimates。 这不足以作为论文 pivot 的主贡献——improvement 太小且仅在 small n 显著。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Robustness to Misspecified Subgroups\",\n    \"description\": \"EC-HTE 在 subgroup structure noisy/overlapping 或与 true structure 不 aligned 时的表现。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"echte_rmse_correct_subgroups\": 0.035,\n      \"echte_rmse_noisy_subgroups_10pct_noise\": 0.038,\n      \"echte_rmse_noisy_subgroups_30pct_noise\": 0.048,\n      \"echte_rmse_misaligned_subgroups\": 0.055,\n      \"global_rmse_misaligned_subgroups\": 0.042,\n      \"echte_worse_than_global_at_noise_pct\": 25,\n      \"hb_shrinkage_at_30pct_noise\": 0.72,\n      \"hb_recovery_vs_mle_at_30pct_noise_pct\": 8\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 15: Robustness to Subgroup Misspecification\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"condition\",\n          \"echte_hb_rmse\",\n          \"echte_mle_rmse\",\n          \"global_rmse\",\n          \"echte_vs_global_pct\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"correct subgroups\",\n            0.035,\n            0.036,\n            0.04,\n            \"-12.5%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"10% noise\",\n            0.038,\n            0.04,\n            0.04,\n            \"-5.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20% noise\",\n            0.042,\n            0.046,\n            0.04,\n            \"+5.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"30% noise\",\n            0.048,\n            0.054,\n            0.04,\n            \"+20.0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"misaligned subgroups\",\n            0.055,\n            0.062,\n            0.042,\n            \"+31.0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Robustness 结果对 worst 档有 mixed implications。Negative：EC-HTE 不是 \\\"never worse than global\\\"——在 misspecified subgroups 下可以更差。Positive：HB partial pooling 的 adaptive shrinkage 确实在 work，只是不够 fully salvage。论文必须讨论这个 limitation 并建议 practitioners 用 diagnostic criterion + domain knowledge 验证 subgroup choice。 这也 weakens Claim 2 的 \\\"applicable to any CATE estimator\\\" 部分——需要加 caveat。\\n\\n\\nSubgroup misspecification 对 EC-HTE 的打击比对 global 更大——因为 EC-HTE 依赖 subgroup structure 来 estimate per-group confusion matrices，而 global 对 subgroup 定义 robust by construction。在 10% noise 下降幅小（8%），但 30% noise 下 EC-HTE RMSE 增加 37%， 且在 25% noise 处 EC-HTE 反转为 worse than global。Misaligned subgroups（true heterogeneity 沿 dimension A，correction 沿 dimension B）更严重——EC-HTE 比 global 差 31%。HB partial pooling 在高 noise 下确实 shrink toward global（shrinkage 0.72），部分 mitigate 了问题 （比 MLE stratified 好 8%），但不够 fully recover。这暴露了 EC-HTE 的 Achilles heel： 需要 correct subgroup specification，而在实践中这可能需要 domain expertise。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Causal Forest Integration\",\n    \"description\": \"EC-HTE post-hoc correction on CausalForestDML leaf-level estimates， vs naive forest vs globally-corrected forest。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"echte_forest_rmse\": 0.038,\n      \"global_forest_rmse\": 0.036,\n      \"naive_forest_rmse\": 0.045,\n      \"echte_forest_coverage\": 0.85,\n      \"global_forest_coverage\": 0.83,\n      \"naive_forest_coverage\": 0.75,\n      \"echte_forest_vs_global_improvement_pct\": -5.6,\n      \"variance_adjusted_ci_width_ratio\": 1.35,\n      \"leaf_level_correction_convergence_rate\": 0.78\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Table 16: Causal Forest Integration Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"rmse\",\n          \"bias\",\n          \"coverage\",\n          \"ci_width_mean\",\n          \"convergence_rate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Naive Forest\",\n            0.045,\n            0.032,\n            0.75,\n            0.08,\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Global-Corrected Forest\",\n            0.036,\n            0.018,\n            0.83,\n            0.1,\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EC-HTE Forest (leaf-level)\",\n            0.038,\n            0.012,\n            0.85,\n            0.135,\n            0.78\n          ],\n          [\n            \"EC-HTE Forest (subgroup-level)\",\n            0.037,\n            0.015,\n            0.84,\n            0.12,\n            0.95\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Causal forest integration 不是可行的 pivot direction（Angle C fails for exp-011）。 Leaf-level correction 的 variance-bias tradeoff 不利，convergence issues 更是 red flag。 Subgroup-level correction applied to forest（而非 leaf-level）表现稍好（RMSE 0.037 vs 0.036）， 接近 global 但没有 clear win。建议在论文中不把 forest integration 作为 contribution， 仅在 discussion 中提到 \\\"straightforward extension exists but requires careful variance management\\\"。\\n\\nCausal forest integration 在 worst 档下表现差于 global correction。原因：forest 的 leaf 已经是数据驱动的 subgroups，与手工定义的 correction subgroups 不 aligned。Leaf-level correction 每个 leaf 的 sample size 太小（典型 50–200 observations），confusion matrix 估计 noisy，variance inflation（CI width +35%）抵消了 bias reduction。Global correction 在 forest setting 下更 robust——forest 自身的 adaptive partitioning 已经 partially account for heterogeneity。EC-HTE 的 RMSE 反而比 global 高 5.6%。收敛率只有 78%（22% 的 MC runs 中 leaf-level correction 的 matrix inversion 出现 numerical issues）。 这意味着 Claim 2 的 \\\"causal forest integration\\\" 部分在 worst 档下 fails。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":990,"startLine":1,"totalLines":990}}}
